"---
name: widget
description: Load when making widgets.
---

# @acme/widget

Widgets, made correctly.

Not for: gadgets.

## Use it

\`\`\`ts
const w = makeWidget(3)
\`\`\`

From \`examples/basic.ts\`.

## Import from

| Import | For |
| --- | --- |
| \`@acme/widget\` | \`makeWidget\`, the widget types |
| \`@acme/widget/extra\` | extra helpers |

## Rules

- Always pass a size.
- Never mutate a widget.

## Rely on

- Making a widget is synchronous.

## Common mistakes

| Instead of | Do this |
| --- | --- |
| \`new Widget()\` | \`makeWidget(size)\` |

## Verify

1. Run the type check.
2. Run the tests.

Report any check you could not run, and any assumption you made.

## Go deeper

- [Sizes in depth](https://github.com/acme/widget/blob/main/GUIDE.md#sizes)
- [Every public signature](https://github.com/acme/widget/blob/main/skills/widget/references/api.md)

## Authority

Target \`@acme/widget@1.2.3\`. The installed package's exports and type declarations are the API: do not invent exports, options or return values. Behaviour is established by its tests and examples. If this skill and the code disagree, say so rather than guessing.
"
`;

